      "message": "In the signature for `launch()`, the type hint for `gdb_port` is written as:\n\n```python\ngdb_port: Optional[int] \u003d 3333,\n\n```\n\n**Recommendation:**\n`Optional[int]` implies the value is expected to be either an `int` or `None`. However, `argparse` uses `type\u003dint` with a default of `3333`, so it will essentially always pass an `int`. While the inline logic (`if gdb_port and gdb_port \u003e 0:`) perfectly handles both `0` and `None` safely, it is cleaner Python style to just type it as `gdb_port: int \u003d 3333` unless `None` is specifically intended to be passed by an internal caller.",
